From a1f37e44f9d8c92e6bf223e9034f3cc7833cf048 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Null-H3x <null-h3x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 23:39:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Paranoia-harden run_summary: bulletproof against
 killed-run artifacts

Static + adversarial audit of the summary path ahead of a multi-day GPU
scan. Three fixes:

1. UTF-8 crash (HIGH): _scan_near_misses opened shards as strict utf-8, so
   a worker killed mid-multibyte-char left a partial line that raised
   UnicodeDecodeError -- NOT an OSError, so it slipped the except and would
   have crashed the summary AFTER the run completed. Now opens with
   errors='replace' and the per-shard except catches Exception, so one
   unreadable shard is skipped, never fatal.

2. Fallback render: write_run_summary body split into a guarded render; if
   rendering throws for any reason, a completed run still gets a minimal
   honest file (error, coverage, survivors, scope line) instead of nothing.
   The whole point is that a finished multi-day run ALWAYS leaves a
   reviewable artifact.

3. GPU n_errors: replaced misleading getattr(args,'_grand_errors',0) with
   an explicit 0 + comment (the GPU pipeline has no per-seed error bucket).

Adversarial battery (9/9): invalid-utf8 shard, truncated header, empty
max_hits, non-numeric zipf, all-zeros run (div-by-zero traps), backwards
seed range, missing corpus, >100% coverage clamp. Math audit: every
division guarded (max(...,1)/max(...,1e-9)/conditional), coverage capped
at 1.0, seeds/combo floored at 0, ETA gated on rate>0. Suite 9/9.
---
 eyestat/eyestat_gpu_runner.py |  5 ++-
 eyestat/eyestat_runner.py     | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/eyestat/eyestat_gpu_runner.py b/eyestat/eyestat_gpu_runner.py
index 153af44..3ae373a 100755
--- a/eyestat/eyestat_gpu_runner.py
+++ b/eyestat/eyestat_gpu_runner.py
@@ -1129,7 +1129,10 @@ def run_gpu_brute_force(args):
             seed_start=args.seed_start, seed_end=args.seed_end,
             threshold=args.threshold,
             n_tried=grand_tried, n_hits=grand_hits,
-            n_errors=getattr(args, "_grand_errors", 0),
+            # GPU pipeline has no per-seed error bucket (a seed is filtered
+            # or scored, never "errored" the way a CPU worker chunk can);
+            # 0 is the honest value here, not a placeholder.
+            n_errors=0,
             est_total_keys=(args.seed_end - args.seed_start),
             elapsed=elapsed, total_units=1,
             completed_units=1, all_top_hits=all_top_hits,
