Context: claude.ai login/email verification is unreliable under load, so
once the box is booted into Ubuntu the scan must be self-sufficient — no
ability to paste errors to Claude interactively. Two additions make the
handoff complete:

  • run.py --doctor: reconstructs what a run actually did from shard
    filenames alone (they encode each shard's seed range). Reports seeds
    covered, fraction of the Park-Miller space, and detects GAPS in
    coverage — the fingerprint of a skipped-shard short run — then scans
    the run log for tell-tale error/skip/validate/done lines. Needs no
    network. Verified on gap, contiguous, and empty-dir cases.

  • PRNG_SCAN_FIELD_MANUAL.md: standalone offline runbook — launch
    sequence, live monitoring, the short-run diagnosis flow, a
    failure-mode table, interrupted-run recovery, and what a clean null
    means (with the honest-scope reminder). Lives in the repo so it's on
    the Ubuntu box when Claude isn't reachable.

Selftest suite unaffected: 9/9.
